<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d6" for="edge" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="edge" attr.name="keywords" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="edge" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d3" for="edge" attr.name="weight" attr.type="double" />
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;KIRKCUDBRIGHT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kirkcudbright is a rural town in 17th century Scotland where the trial of Bessie Broun took place, known for its climate of fear and superstition."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BESSIE BROUN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bessie Broun is a humble woman accused of witchcraft and consorting with the devil, a central figure in the trial."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMMISSION OF JUSTICIARY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Commission of Justiciary is a powerful instrument of justice in Scotland, established in 1597 to investigate and prosecute serious crimes."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LORD ADVOCATE SIR JOHN FLETCHER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lord Advocate Sir John Fletcher is a seasoned jurist appointed as the presiding judge in Bessie Broun's trial, known for his reputation of fairness and integrity."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KIRKCALDY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kirkcaldy is a town in Scotland where the trial of Bessie Broun took place in 1662, during the height of witch hysteria."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THOMAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Thomas is the stern-faced prosecutor in Bessie Broun's trial, holding a parchment with the wax seal of the local lord."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WITCHCRAFT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Witchcraft is the accusation against Bessie Broun, involving curses, conjuring storms, and making a pact with the devil."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEVIL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The devil is a central figure in the accusations against Bessie Broun, representing supernatural evil and malevolence."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEALER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Healer is the profession of Bessie Broun, known for her knowledge of natural remedies and her ability to cure ailments."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WITCH HYSTERIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Witch hysteria is a period of intense fear and suspicion surrounding witchcraft, reaching a fever pitch in 1662."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;17TH CENTURY SCOTLAND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"17th century Scotland is the setting of the events, characterized by religious strife and political upheaval."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROTESTANT REFORMATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Protestant Reformation is a historical event that fueled the climate of fear and superstition in 17th century Scotland."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RURAL TOWN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rural town is a general term for the setting of Kirkcudbright, where the trial of Bessie Broun took place."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TOWN SQUARE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Town square is the location where the trial of Bessie Broun took place in Kirkcaldy in 1662."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ROLLING HILLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rolling hills are part of the Scottish countryside where the villagers of Kirkcaldy gather in the town square."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOCAL LORD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Local lord is the holder of the wax seal on the parchment held by the prosecutor, symbolizing authority."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WITNESSES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Witnesses are individuals who testify in Bessie Broun's trial, providing accounts of her alleged supernatural abilities."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPECTRAL EVIDENCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Spectral evidence is a type of testimony used in Bessie Broun's trial, involving dreams and visions."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NATURAL REMEDIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Natural remedies are the methods used by Bessie Broun to cure ailments, which are central to her defense."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COERCION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Coercion is a key theme in Bessie Broun's defense, as she argues that her patients gave their consent freely."&lt;SEP&gt;"Coercion is mentioned as the opposite of the voluntary agreement given by individuals."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TUMULTUOUS HISTORY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tumultuous history is a description of Scotland's past, marked by religious strife and political upheaval."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CRIMES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Crimes are the serious offenses investigated and prosecuted by the Commission of Justiciary, including witchcraft and treason."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROSECUTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Prosecution is the legal team presenting evidence against Bessie Broun in her trial."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEFENSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Defense is the legal team representing Bessie Broun in her trial, arguing her innocence and the validity of her natural remedies."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRIVY COUNCIL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Privy Council is the governing body that granted the Commission of Justiciary its authority to investigate and try cases."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRIALS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Trials are the judicial proceedings in which Bessie Broun is accused and defended."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NATURAL WORLD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Natural world is the domain of Bessie Broun's knowledge, from which she draws her remedies and cures."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUPERNATURAL ABILITIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Supernatural abilities are the accusations against Bessie Broun, including her alleged powers to curse and conjure storms."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONSENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Consent is a key theme in Bessie Broun's defense, as she argues that her patients gave their consent freely."&lt;SEP&gt;"Consent refers to the voluntary agreement given by individuals to receive the speaker's remedies."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CURSES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Curses are part of the accusations against Bessie Broun, suggesting she has the power to harm others."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STORMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Storms are part of the accusations against Bessie Broun, suggesting she has the power to summon them."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REMEDIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Remedies are the natural cures provided by Bessie Broun, which are central to her defense."&lt;SEP&gt;"Remedies refer to the treatments or methods used by the speaker to help others."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INQUISITION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Inquisition is a term that could describe the intense scrutiny and questioning of Bessie Broun during her trial."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JUSTICE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Justice is the overarching theme of the Commission of Justiciary's role in Bessie Broun's trial."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BESSIE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bessie is a healer who provides remedies to those seeking her aid, and her actions are questioned during a trial."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VILLAGERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The villagers are a group of people who seek Bessie's help and give their consent for her remedies."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRIAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A trial is mentioned where the villagers' actions and consent are being questioned."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;I&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The speaker is a person who seeks to explain their actions and the consent of others."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THOSE WHO HAVE SOUGHT MY AID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A group of people who have sought the speaker's aid, referred to as 'those who have sought my aid'."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VILLAGERS'">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The villagers are a group of people who seek Bessie's help and give their consent for her remedies."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WILLINGLY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Willingly describes the voluntary nature of the individuals seeking aid."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FULL KNOWLEDGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Full knowledge refers to the awareness of the individuals about the remedies provided."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WHISPERED AMONG THEMSELVES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Whispering is an event where the villagers discuss among themselves."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONFUSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Confusion is a state of mind experienced by the villagers due to the situation."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TIMES OF NEED&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Times of need refer to occasions when the villagers required assistance."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACCEPTED HER REMEDIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Acceptance of remedies is an event where the villagers agree to the treatments provided by Bessie."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DOUBTS GREW&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Doubts growing is an event where the villagers' uncertainties increase during the trial."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KIRKCUDRY&quot;">
      <data key="d2">cb-0241</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kirkcudry, a town in Scotland, experienced a period of intense witch hysteria in 1662, leading to the trial of Bessie Broun."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <edge source="&quot;BESSIE BROUN&quot;" target="&quot;WITCHCRAFT&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Bessie Broun is accused of witchcraft, including curses, conjuring storms, and making a pact with the devil."</data>
      <data key="d5">"accusation, supernatural abilities"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0241</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BESSIE BROUN&quot;" target="&quot;DEVIL&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Bessie Broun is accused of consorting with the devil, a central figure in the accusations of witchcraft."</data>
      <data key="d5">"supernatural association, malevolence"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0241</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BESSIE BROUN&quot;" target="&quot;HEALER&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Bessie Broun is a healer known for her knowledge of natural remedies and her ability to cure ailments, providing help to those in need."</data>
      <data key="d5">"help, natural remedies"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0241</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BESSIE BROUN&quot;" target="&quot;COMMISSION OF JUSTICIARY&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The Commission of Justiciary plays a crucial role in gathering evidence, interrogating witnesses, and overseeing Bessie Broun's trial."</data>
      <data key="d5">"investigation, prosecution"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0241</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BESSIE BROUN&quot;" target="&quot;LORD ADVOCATE SIR JOHN FLETCHER&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Lord Advocate Sir John Fletcher is appointed as the presiding judge in Bessie Broun's trial, ensuring a fair and just proceeding."</data>
      <data key="d5">"judicial role, fairness"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0241</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;KIRKCALDY&quot;" target="&quot;WITCH HYSTERIA&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Kirkcaldy, another town in Scotland, also experienced a period of intense witch hysteria in 1662, leading to the trial of Bessie Broun."</data>
      <data key="d5">"hysteria, fear"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0241</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;WITCH HYSTERIA&quot;" target="&quot;KIRKCUDRY&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Kirkcudry, a town in Scotland, experienced a period of intense witch hysteria in 1662, leading to the trial of Bessie Broun."</data>
      <data key="d5">"hysteria, fear"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0241</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;CONSENT&quot;" target="&quot;REMEDIES&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The remedies are provided with the consent of the individuals seeking aid."</data>
      <data key="d5">"agreement, treatment"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0241</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;CONSENT&quot;" target="&quot;VILLAGERS'">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The villagers have given their consent, either explicitly or implicitly, to the remedies provided by Bessie."</data>
      <data key="d5">"consent, acceptance"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0241</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;REMEDIES&quot;" target="&quot;THOSE WHO HAVE SOUGHT MY AID&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Those who have sought aid have received remedies from the speaker."</data>
      <data key="d5">"treatment, aid"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0241</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;REMEDIES&quot;" target="&quot;VILLAGERS'">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The villagers have accepted the remedies provided by Bessie."</data>
      <data key="d5">"acceptance, treatment"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0241</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BESSIE&quot;" target="&quot;VILLAGERS&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Bessie provides remedies to the villagers, who give their consent for her treatments."</data>
      <data key="d5">"healing, consent"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0241</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;VILLAGERS&quot;" target="&quot;TRIAL&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The villagers' actions and consent are being questioned during the trial."</data>
      <data key="d5">"doubt, questioning"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0241</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;TRIAL&quot;" target="&quot;DOUBTS GREW&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The growing doubts of the villagers are a result of the ongoing trial involving Bessie and the remedies provided."</data>
      <data key="d5">"trial, doubt"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0241</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;I&quot;" target="&quot;THOSE WHO HAVE SOUGHT MY AID&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The speaker explains that those who have sought their aid have done so willingly and with full knowledge of the remedies provided."</data>
      <data key="d5">"explanation, consent"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0241</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;VILLAGERS'" target="&quot;WHISPERED AMONG THEMSELVES&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The villagers whisper among themselves, discussing the situation involving Bessie and the trial."</data>
      <data key="d5">"discussion, whispering"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0241</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;VILLAGERS'" target="&quot;TIMES OF NEED&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The villagers have sought aid in times of need, indicating situations where they required assistance."</data>
      <data key="d5">"need, aid"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0241</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;VILLAGERS'" target="&quot;ACCEPTED HER REMEDIES&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The villagers have accepted Bessie's remedies in times of need, showing their trust in her."</data>
      <data key="d5">"trust, acceptance"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0241</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;WHISPERED AMONG THEMSELVES&quot;" target="&quot;CONFUSION&quot;">
      <data key="d3">6.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Whispering among the villagers leads to confusion about the situation involving Bessie and the trial."</data>
      <data key="d5">"confusion, discussion"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0241</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ACCEPTED HER REMEDIES&quot;" target="&quot;DOUBTS GREW&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The acceptance of remedies by the villagers leads to growing doubts during the trial."</data>
      <data key="d5">"doubt, acceptance"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0241</data>
    </edge>
  </graph>
</graphml>
